{"data": [{"author_id": "1659439170883026945", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:54:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120319323667583060"], "id": "2120319323667583060", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition 26.3% to 40.0% is a big jump. For picking a model per agent I'd want the categories split out too, because in our own browser-agent test the composite was useful for ranking, and only the separate columns told us what would fail.", "url": "https://x.com/jackrudenko/status/2120319323667583060"}, {"author_id": "1754759209940647936", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:48:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120302489648173142"], "id": "2120302489648173142", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition Going from 26.3% to 40% is a real jump. Six in ten runs needing an engineer to finish them is the number teams will actually budget around.", "url": "https://x.com/teamnebulaai/status/2120302489648173142"}, {"author_id": "1855662384", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:01:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120290825150013806"], "id": "2120290825150013806", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 72, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition https://t.co/F9NKJGBr6R\n\nAgain, not sure why you guys chose to run it in your Devin harness.\n\nIf the results in AGY are worse, post those since its what most users would experience anyways.", "url": "https://x.com/Antreges/status/2120290825150013806"}, {"author_id": "1466416677713854477", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:08:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120262455716942008"], "id": "2120262455716942008", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 188, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition 40 from 26 is a big jump", "url": "https://x.com/Laz01L/status/2120262455716942008"}, {"author_id": "2114261495278391296", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:23:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120235948239892864"], "id": "2120235948239892864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition Cognition 表示，Google 的 Gemini 4 Carbon 现已可用于 Devin Desktop 和 Devin CLI，在其 FrontierCode 2.0 基准测试中得分 40.0%，高于 Gemini 4 Argon 的 26.3%。", "url": "https://x.com/aixindongjing/status/2120235948239892864"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:03:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120230933295144970"], "id": "2120230933295144970", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 51, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition A jump on a coding benchmark is encouraging, but the test that matters is a long project with real constraints. If Carbon holds up there, Devin users will feel it in fewer dead ends.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2120230933295144970"}, {"author_id": "1466066870931443716", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:56:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120229052585804026"], "id": "2120229052585804026", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 331, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition please run gemini models in antigravity, otherwise these results are meaningless", "url": "https://x.com/mihai673/status/2120229052585804026"}, {"author_id": "1940716261903568896", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:43:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120225948822069463"], "id": "2120225948822069463", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@luisnhenrich @cognition fair, the 45 is from anthropic's own setup and the 40 from devin's, so it's not apples to apples. would love to see both run in the same harness", "url": "https://x.com/callmedraxxx/status/2120225948822069463"}, {"author_id": "2054274215872733184", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:26:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120221598099595700"], "id": "2120221598099595700", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@callmedraxxx @cognition worth checking the harness too before comparing the 40 and the 45. if the two scores come from different agent setups, part of that gap is the harness rather than the model.", "url": "https://x.com/luisnhenrich/status/2120221598099595700"}, {"author_id": "3486300979", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:14:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120218578091639197"], "id": "2120218578091639197", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition 26.3% to 40% in a month looks incremental. It isn't. Agent runs compound: a 50-step task at 98% per step finishes 36% of the time, at 99% it's 61%. One point of per-step reliability almost doubles what actually ships. That's the whole agent race.", "url": "https://x.com/mikesentora/status/2120218578091639197"}, {"author_id": "1471034497500172290", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:13:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120218246032785800"], "id": "2120218246032785800", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 161, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition 26.3 to 40 in a single version jump. somebody at google had a good month", "url": "https://x.com/AgentikHQ/status/2120218246032785800"}, {"author_id": "1396149219728236546", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:22:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120205496154202133"], "id": "2120205496154202133", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 84, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition New SWE when?\nUpdated fusion when?", "url": "https://x.com/dkdkskssnskdnx4/status/2120205496154202133"}, {"author_id": "1709375573200613376", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:19:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120204674640843197"], "id": "2120204674640843197", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 237, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition 26.3% to 40% on FrontierCode in one release is a big jump, curious how Carbon holds up on longer tasks.", "url": "https://x.com/ramkumar_9301/status/2120204674640843197"}, {"author_id": "2071740446292791296", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:16:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120203946593509405"], "id": "2120203946593509405", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@camperaigg @cognition Can we get it with fusion? I noticed Argon isn’t available with fusion", "url": "https://x.com/AnAIRenaissance/status/2120203946593509405"}, {"author_id": "1940716261903568896", "conversation_id": "2120196422360506385", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:15:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120203600471453991"], "id": "2120203600471453991", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 276, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition nice jump. any cost per task numbers? anthropic says fable 5.2 high gets ~45% on the same test, so if carbon is way cheaper that 5 point gap might not matter", "url": "https://x.com/callmedraxxx/status/2120203600471453991"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1659439170883026945", "name": "Jack Rudenko", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 202, "following_count": 677, "like_count": 1731, "listed_count": 2, "media_count": 382, "tweet_count": 1966}, "username": "jackrudenko"}, {"id": "1754759209940647936", "name": "Team Nebula", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 165, "following_count": 114, "like_count": 1238, "listed_count": 5, "media_count": 146, "tweet_count": 1826}, "username": "teamnebulaai"}, {"id": "1855662384", "name": "Antryg", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 14, "following_count": 59, "like_count": 6665, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 3, "tweet_count": 24}, "username": "Antreges"}, {"id": "1466416677713854477", "name": "Mads", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 125, "following_count": 350, "like_count": 374, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 31, "tweet_count": 1016}, "username": "Laz01L"}, {"id": "2114261495278391296", "name": "AI 新动静", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 2, "following_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 32, "tweet_count": 517}, "username": "aixindongjing"}, {"id": "46498861", "name": "Raúl Nogales 🇪🇸🇺🇸", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 14200, "following_count": 167, "like_count": 3792, "listed_count": 103, "media_count": 689, "tweet_count": 13951}, "username": "raulnogales"}, {"id": "1466066870931443716", "name": "Mihai", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 1699, "following_count": 5923, "like_count": 76972, "listed_count": 41, "media_count": 1872, "tweet_count": 12389}, "username": "mihai673"}, {"id": "1940716261903568896", "n